  "reason": "The records provide several partial clues: R7 uses in situ high-temperature vacuum exposure of an equiatomic HEA and observes element-selective surface reaction and bulk depletion; R10 reports elemental segregation to internal interfaces; R12 describes temperature- and deformation-dependent atomic redistribution in an HEA; and R14 shows preferential elemental loss during energetic processing. Other records establish active lattice diffusion, surface-energy effects, or high-temperature simulations of nanoscale HEAs. However, none studies AuCoCuNiPt nanoparticles or identifies surface-energy-driven Au/Cu segregation, reshaping-enhanced diffusion, and subsequent evaporation. Thus the set points generally toward thermally activated, element-selective redistribution but would require a substantial new idea to formulate the later paper's specific nanoparticle intervention and mechanism."
